decisions:
  - id: P8-D12
    decision: 'Human signing via key file + CLI for founder-only 8.0, as an ACCEPTED RISK (Aegis rated critical: an agent with Bash can read the key and self-approve). Amends TD-2026-10-14-735 §4 (S4 custodian before multi-instance runs) for solo use only. Revisit trigger: before any second human, shared fabric, or 8.1.'
    rationale: 'Founder chose speed over Touch ID prompts; recorded with zero-UX-cost mitigations: signed registry rows, kernel-owned log namespaces no principal may append, deny rules on key paths.'
  - id: P8-D13
    decision: Oracles run under a macOS sandbox-exec profile first (deny ~/.gnomon, ~/.ssh, keychain, egress; scrubbed env; read-only worktree), rootless containers later. ACCEPTED RISK amending TD-2026-10-14-735 §7 for solo 8.0; same revisit trigger.
    rationale: No extra install now; weaker isolation acknowledged.
  - id: P8-D14
    decision: Warpline PICKs are signed by stable roster agents (keys minted once by the founder); sessions borrow the credential and link session to strand by causes[]; the kernel never mints.
    rationale: 'Arky: kernel minting imports the Warpline engine, bypasses the human gate (keys.ts:441) and pins the signing epoch; per-session keys break one-key-one-notebook-owner.'
  - id: P8-D15
    decision: The reviewer oracle runs on the founder's subscription as a claude -p turn under the budget fuse
    rationale: Keeps the subscription-only preflight intact.
